    "text": "1. Chest tightness or shortness of breath during exertion\n“Chest tightness or shortness of breath that builds with exertion and fades when you rest,” says Dr London. “This one isn’t subtle on paper. It’s subtle because of how easy it is to explain away, out of shape, carrying extra weight, bad allergy season.”",
